From e7ac0031ef21e087d68e4a7915b4c27bb7ee6f15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DMV11: switch packs E101/E113 and primary MOP boot (PDP-11)

Patch 18 v3 (replaces v1 and v2).  The DMV11 switch packs of
EK-DMVQM-UG-003 (Figure 2-6, Tables 2-6 and 4-5) per DMV line, every
switch ON by default as in the manual:
  SET DMVn MODE=...            mode (E101 SW1, SW6-8)
  SET DMVn TRIBUTARY=n         tributary address/password (E113)
  SET DMVn BOOTUNIT={0|1}      unit number for booting (E101 SW2)
  SET DMVn {NO}POWERONBOOT     power-on boot (E101 SW4)
  SET DMVn {NO}REMOTELOAD      remote load detect (E101 SW5)
  SHOW DMVn SWITCHES
In the PDP-11 simulator the primary MOP boot: remote load detect, power-on
boot (BOOT DMVn), invoke primary MOP.
  SET DMVn PROGRAM={SECONDARY|TERTIARY|SYSTEM}  (simulator setting) MOP
  program type requested; SYSTEM loads the LOAD FILE directly.
v2: DTR rule of EK-DMV11-TM-001 Appendix D for remote load detect; MOP
debug; fix for all DMC/DMR/DMP/DMV types: a sent DDCMP maintenance
message was never returned to the host (VMS NCP LOAD NODE hung).
v3: SET DMVn PROGRAM; the started program gets SP 774 (stack below 1000).
Multipoint MOP messages carry the tributary address.

Tested: VMS V4.7 on a MicroVAX II (LOAD NODE) loads a PDP-11/73: a
secondary loader (default) and, with PROGRAM=SYSTEM, a 32 KB load file
(remwrt) that then runs; tests/dmv11_boot T1-T6 pass.

